    "result_text": "All tests pass (`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full suite is green).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented idempotent create for `POST /api/owners` with **zero changes to existing functions** \u2014 only new, small, cohesive units plus wiring, keeping structural impact minimal.\n\n**What happens now:** when a create carries an `Idempotency-Key` header whose value was already used, the endpoint returns the originally created owner with **200** instead of creating a duplicate (which would otherwise 409).\n\n**New classes (each tiny, near-zero surrounding complexity):**\n- `IdempotencyStore` (Spring `@Component`) \u2014 in-memory `key \u2192 OwnerDto` map; distinct keys never collide.\n- `IdempotencyToken` (record) \u2014 carries the header value between steps as a dedicated variable type (unambiguous `Out`/`@Val` matching).\n- `CheckIdempotencyKey` \u2014 new first pipeline step: reads the optional header via `ServerHttpConnection`, publishes the token, and on a seen key throws `IdempotentReplayException` to short-circuit the whole pipeline.\n- `RecordIdempotencyKey` \u2014 runs after `save` (owner has its id, still under transaction governance), builds the DTO and stores it against the key.\n- `IdempotentReplayException` + `IdempotentReplayExceptionHandler` \u2014 escalation that responds 200 with the stored DTO (no DB access needed, since the DTO was built under the original governance \u2014 important because `open-in-view=false` and pets are eagerly fetched).\n\n**Wiring:** added two steps to `owners.POST.yml` and one escalation YAML.\n\n**Design choices worth noting:**\n- Used the **escalation mechanism** (throwing a checked exception) to short-circuit rather than a `@Flow` branch, because in OfficeFloor invoking a flow does not suppress the step's `next`, so a flow couldn't cleanly skip the rest of the create pipeline.\n- The replay stores/returns a fully-built `OwnerDto` so the handler runs without a DB session, sidestepping lazy-loading issues.\n- A blank/absent key is a no-op, so all existing keyless creates are unaffected.",
