    "probe_text": "Here is the complete ordered trace of `POST /api/owners`. The endpoint is defined in `owners.POST.yml` as a 22-step pipeline (one guard + 21 functions). I've marked each as a **validation** (can reject the request) or a **side-effect** (mutates state, the entity, or the outside world).\n\n## Gate (before any step)\n\n0. **Authorization** \u2014 `composition.authorize: hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')`. Caller lacking the role is rejected (`AuthorizationDeniedException` handler) before the pipeline runs.\n\n## Pipeline steps, in order\n\n1. **`CheckIdempotencyKey`** \u2014 reads the optional `Idempotency-Key` header, publishes it as a token. *Validation/short-circuit:* if that key already produced an owner, throws `IdempotentReplayException` and replays the stored owner (200) instead of creating.\n\n2. **`RequireOwnerFields`** *(validation)* \u2014 reads the `@RequestBody` (the only step that does), rejects with 400 (`MissingOwnerFieldsException`) if any of `firstName`, `lastName`, `city`, `telephone` is null/blank, or if **both** `addressLine1` and the flat `address` are blank. Publishes the body for later steps.\n\n3. **`NormalizeOwnerTelephone`** *(side-effect + validation)* \u2014 converts `telephone` to E.164 in place (assumes `+61`, drops a leading `0`, strips punctuation). Rejects 400 if it can't form 8\u201315 digits.\n\n4. **`ValidateTelephoneLength`** *(validation)* \u2014 for `+61` requires 9 national digits, for `+1` requires 10; wrong length \u2192 400. Other country codes pass.\n\n5. **`NormalizeOwnerEmail`** *(side-effect + validation)* \u2014 if an email is present: rejects 400 (`InvalidOwnerEmailException`) if it fails the regex **or** its domain is disposable (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`); otherwise lower-cases it in place. Missing email is left alone.\n\n6. **`NormalizeOwnerAddress`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 canonicalizes the address in place: trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`. Prefers structured `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` (composing `address` from them), else normalizes the flat `address`.\n\n7. **`ValidatePostcode`** *(validation)* \u2014 if a postcode is present: must be 4 digits, and for known cities must fall in range (Sydney 2000\u20132099, Melbourne 3000\u20133099, Brisbane 4000\u20134099); else 400 (`InvalidPostcodeException`). Unknown city \u2192 any 4 digits OK. Missing postcode passes.\n\n8. **`RejectFutureRegistrationDate`** *(validation)* \u2014 if `registrationDate` is after the server's today \u2192 400 (`FutureRegistrationDateException`). Missing date passes.\n\n*(Transaction governance begins here \u2014 steps 9 through 22 all run under `govern: [ transaction ]`, committing once at the end.)*\n\n9. **`RejectDuplicateIdentity`** *(validation)* \u2014 scans all non-deleted owners; if the full identity key (E.164 telephone `|` lower-cased email `|` computed householdId) exactly matches an existing owner \u2192 409 (`DuplicateIdentityException`).\n\n10. **`RejectDuplicateHousehold`** *(validation)* \u2014 computes householdId (last name + postcode); if it already belongs to a non-deleted owner \u2192 409 (`DuplicateHouseholdException`). Skipped when `sharesHousehold=true` or when there's no postcode.\n\n11. **`RejectCityAtCapacity`** *(validation)* \u2014 if the city (compared case-insensitively, whitespace-collapsed) already has \u2265 50 owners \u2192 409 (`CityAtCapacityException`).\n\n12. **`RejectDailyLimit`** *(validation)* \u2014 rolls the effective registration date onto a business day; if \u2265 100 owners already registered that day \u2192 429 (`DailyLimitExceededException`).\n\n13. **`BuildOwner`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 maps the DTO to an `Owner` entity; sets its `registrationDate` to the effective date (supplied or today) **rolled forward onto a business day** (weekends/holidays skipped).\n\n14. **`AssignCustomerCode`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 sets `customerCode` = `<REGION>-<HASH8>`, region from postcode (20xx\u2192NSW, 30xx\u2192VIC, 40xx\u2192QLD) then city, else UNKNOWN; HASH8 = first 8 hex chars of SHA-256 over `telephone + lastName`.\n\n15. **`DeduplicateCustomerCode`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 if that code already exists among current owners, appends `-<n>` with the smallest `n \u2265 2` making it unique.\n\n16. **`AssignHousehold`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 sets `householdId` deterministically from last name + postcode (null if no postcode).\n\n17. **`AssignNamesakeCount`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 sets `namesakeCount` to how many existing owners share this first+last name (case-insensitive).\n\n18. **`FlagPossibleDuplicate`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 sets `possibleDuplicateOf` to the id of an existing owner in the same household with a *different* telephone. Skipped when `sharesHousehold=true` or no household.\n\n19. **`SaveOwner`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 persists the owner via the repository (assigns its id).\n\n20. **`RecordIdempotencyKey`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 builds the response DTO (applying the household gold-tier points bump and bulk-signup warning) and stores it against the `Idempotency-Key` so a later repeat replays it.\n\n21. **`AuditOwnerCreated`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 writes an `AUDIT` log line with id, customerCode, registrationDate, membershipLevel, membershipNumber (recomputing the household gold tier for the log).\n\n22. **`RespondWithOwnerCreated`** *(side-effect / response)* \u2014 maps the owner to `OwnerDto`, applies the household gold-tier bump and bulk-signup warning, and returns **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}` and the DTO body.\n\n## Notes worth flagging\n\n- **The household gold-tier + membership recompute is applied three separate times** (steps 20, 21, 22), each independently via `HouseholdTier.applyGold` \u2014 the response body, the idempotency-stored copy, and the audit line each recompute it.\n- **Duplicate-household and possible-duplicate logic depend on `householdId`, but the new owner's `householdId` isn't set until step 16** \u2014 after the rejection checks (steps 9\u201310) which recompute it from the request rather than reading it off the entity, so the ordering is consistent but the value is derived twice.\n- **`sharesHousehold=true`** bypasses the household duplicate block (10) and the soft-duplicate flag (18), but does **not** change household assignment (16) \u2014 the owner still gets the shared `householdId`."
  },
